        <h2>Geographic Conditions</h2>

        <p>Malaysia is geographically divided into two main regions, West Malaysia (Peninsular) and East Malaysia (Borneo), separated by the South China Sea. With an equatorial tropical climate, Malaysia has mountains in the west and swampy lowlands in the east, with biodiverse tropical rainforests and a long coastline.</p>

